---
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import Link from '../components/Link.astro';
import { routes, site } from '../data/site';

const email = 'info@partyprintkit.com';
---

<TextPage
  title="Contact PartyPrintKit"
  description="Contact PartyPrintKit: request an occasion or a design, report a file that prints wrong, or ask about using the printables at an event."
  path="/contact/"
  crumb="Contact"
  eyebrow="Contact"
  heading="Get in touch."
  lede="One inbox, read by a person."
>
  <p class="contact-email">
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>What is worth writing about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>A missing occasion or piece.</b> Requests decide what gets drawn next.</li>
    <li><b>A file that prints wrong.</b> Tell us the file name, your paper size and your printer, and it gets fixed rather than explained away.</li>
    <li><b>Using the printables at an event.</b> Schools, libraries and community events are covered by the <Link route={routes.terms} class="text-link" label="terms of use" />, but ask if your case is unusual.</li>
    <li><b>Using a photograph or a sheet elsewhere.</b> Ask first, the answer is usually yes with a credit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Before you write</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about paper weight, scaling and cutting are answered in the{' '}
    <Link route={routes.printingGuide} class="text-link" label="printing guide" />. It covers the
    two settings that cause almost every printing problem.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      There is no contact form on purpose: a form needs a script, a spam filter and somewhere to
      store what you typed. An email address needs none of that.
    </p>
  </div>
</TextPage>

<style>
  .contact-email {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px) !important;
    letter-spacing: -1px;
    margin: 0 0 10px !important;
  }
  .contact-email a { color: var(--teal); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #a7cdc9; }
</style>
